---
description: Django/DRF conventions for PredictRx backend
globs: backend/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---
- Business logic in `services.py`; views stay thin. Use `core.exceptions` error shape.
- Ownership/roles are derived server-side from `request.user`; never trust client-supplied roles.
- Every patient-data read, analysis start, family view, consent change → `apps.audit.services.record(...)`.
- LLM/OCR work runs in Celery; API returns a run/scan ID. Use `idempotency_key` for analysis runs.
- Use `select_related`/`prefetch_related`, `update_fields`, specific exceptions. Read generated migrations before committing.
- Never hard-code model names or keys; use settings/env and `ai/llm/router.py`.
- Logs and traces store redacted text only (`ai/guardrails/pii.py`).
